# Append-only logs: both sides' new lines are wanted, never one instead of the
# other. The `union` merge driver concatenates both, which is exactly right here
# and removes the conflict class entirely.
#
# Measured 2026-08-05: the live capture job ran fine but FAILED to commit —
# concurrent appends from the app and the other bots produced a rebase conflict,
# and every retry then died with "Pulling is not possible because you have
# unmerged files" because nothing aborted the rebase. A day's captures were
# computed and thrown away.
*.csv    merge=union
*.jsonl  merge=union

# API snapshots are REGENERATED WHOLE every run, never appended to. Union-merging
# them would splice two documents into invalid JSON, so they must not inherit any
# future *.json rule. On a concurrent-write conflict the right answer is simply
# "keep the copy this run just computed" — the next run overwrites it anyway.
# The `ours` driver is registered in the workflow (merge.ours.driver = true).
api/*.json     merge=ours
static/*.json  merge=ours
